msgstr "การเข้าสู่ระบบด้วยวลีกู้คืนล้มเหลว"

#. Seedphrase sheet: warning that this is the only time the seedphrase is shown.
msgctxt "seedphrase_only_time"
msgid "⚠️ This is the ONLY time you'll see this."
msgstr "⚠️ นี่เป็นครั้งเดียวที่คุณจะเห็นข้อความนี้"

#. Seed sign-in sheet: placeholder of the seedphrase field (android and windows accept 12 or 24 words).
msgctxt "seedphrase_paste_hint"
msgid "Paste your 12 or 24-word seedphrase here"
msgstr "วางวลีกู้คืน 12 หรือ 24 คำของคุณที่นี่"

#. Seed sign-in sheet: error when Sign in is tapped with an empty seedphrase field.
msgctxt "seedphrase_required"
msgid "Please enter a seedphrase"
msgstr "กรุณาป้อนวลีกู้คืน"

#. Seedphrase sheet: advice to write the seedphrase down and store it safely.
msgctxt "seedphrase_store_safely"
msgid "Write it down and store it somewhere safe. If you lose it, you'll lose access to your account."
msgstr "จดไว้และเก็บในที่ปลอดภัย หากทำหาย คุณจะไม่สามารถเข้าถึงบัญชีของคุณได้"

#. Login: warning when the pasted seedphrase has {count} words instead of 12 or 24.
msgctxt "seedphrase_word_count_warning"
msgid "That's {} word — a seedphrase is 12 or 24 words"
msgid_plural "That's {} words — a seedphrase is 12 or 24 words"
msgstr[0] "นั่นคือ {} คำ — วลีกู้คืนมี 12 หรือ 24 คำ"

#. Seeker/Saga token multiplier: what a verified token gives. It doubles points and the free daily data and referral data grants; it does not grant Pro.
msgctxt "seeker_multiplier_benefit"
msgid "Doubles your points, free daily data and referral data."
msgstr "เพิ่มคะแนน ดาต้าฟรีรายวัน และดาต้าจากการแนะนำของคุณเป็นสองเท่า"

#. Seeker token verification: the wallet holds no Seeker or Saga token. The argument is the end of the wallet address.
msgctxt "seeker_token_not_found"
msgid "No Seeker or Saga token found in wallet …{}"
msgstr "ไม่พบโทเค็น Seeker หรือ Saga ในวอลเล็ต …{}"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "seeker_token_verified"
msgid "Seeker Token Verified!"
msgstr "ยืนยัน Seeker Token สำเร็จ"

#. Seeker token verification failed (wallet app error, the server could not be reached, the signature did not verify, or the token lookup failed).
msgctxt "seeker_verify_failed"
msgid "Couldn't verify the Seeker token. Please try again."
msgstr "ไม่สามารถยืนยันโทเค็น Seeker ได้ โปรดลองอีกครั้ง"

#. Seeker token verification: no Solana wallet app is installed to sign the verification message.
msgctxt "seeker_verify_no_wallet_app"
msgid "No Solana wallet app was found on this device."
msgstr "ไม่พบแอปกระเป๋าเงิน Solana บนอุปกรณ์นี้"

#. Used in Main/Account/BlockedLocations/BlockedLocationsView.swift.
msgctxt "select_country_to_block"
msgid "Select country to block"
msgstr "เลือกประเทศที่จะบล็อก"

#. Connect drawer: accessibility label for the globe icon that opens the provider selection list.
msgctxt "select_location_provider_content_description"
msgid "Select location provider globe"
msgstr "ลูกโลก: เลือกตำแหน่งผู้ให้บริการ"

#. Fallback name for the connect location when the selected location has no name.
msgctxt "selected_location"
msgid "Selected location"
msgstr "ตำแหน่งที่เลือก"

#. Label above the provider the connection will use.
msgctxt "selected_provider"
msgid "Selected provider"
msgstr "ผู้ให้บริการที่เลือก"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "send"
msgid "Send"
msgstr "ส่ง"

#. Feedback screen: support contacts. The first argument is the support email address, the second is the name of the community chat (Discord); both are links.
msgctxt "send_feedback_contact"
msgid "Send us your feedback directly, email us at {0}, or join our {1} for direct support."
msgstr "ส่งความคิดเห็นถึงเราโดยตรง ส่งอีเมลมาที่ {0} หรือเข้าร่วม {1} ของเราเพื่อรับความช่วยเหลือโดยตรง"

#. Settings
msgctxt "send_product_updates"
msgid "Send me product updates"
msgstr "ส่งข้อมูลการอัพเดตผลิตภัณฑ์มาที่ฉัน"

#. Forgot password
msgctxt "send_reset_link"
msgid "Send Reset Link"
msgstr "ส่งลิงก์ตั้งรหัสใหม่"

#. Used in Authenticate/ResetPassword/ResetPasswordView.swift.
msgctxt "send_reset_link_2"
msgid "Send reset link"
msgstr "ส่งลิงก์รีเซ็ต"

#. Instruction to fund the gas key.
msgctxt "send_tao_to_mirror"
msgid "Send about {0} TAO to {1} to cover gas."
msgstr "ส่งประมาณ {0} TAO ไปที่ {1} เพื่อเป็นค่า gas"

#. Used in Main/Feedback/FeedbackView.swift.
msgctxt "send_us_your_feedback_directly_or_join_our"
msgid "Send us your feedback directly or [join our Discord](https://discord.com/invite/RUNZXMwPRK) for direct support."
msgstr "ส่งความคิดเห็นของคุณให้เราโดยตรงหรือ[เข้าร่วม Discord ของเรา](https://discord.com/invite/RUNZXMwPRK) เพื่อรับการสนับสนุนโดยตรง"

#. Reset link sent
msgctxt "sent"
msgid "Sent!"
msgstr "ส่งแล้ว!"

#. Snackbar shown after feedback is sent successfully. Used in Main/Feedback/FeedbackView.swift.
msgctxt "sent_thanks_for_your_feedback"
msgid "Sent! Thanks for your feedback."
msgstr "ส่งแล้ว! ขอบคุณสำหรับข้อเสนอแนะ"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): shown on a row when signing its session out failed.
msgctxt "sessions_action_failed"
msgid "Couldn't sign out this session. Try again."
msgstr "ออกจากระบบเซสชันนี้ไม่ได้ ลองอีกครั้ง"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): body of the confirmation before signing another session out. {device} is the row's device label ("Android") and {place} its approximate location ("Chicago, Illinois, United States"), both inserted as they are, so no case ending or article can attach to them.
msgctxt "sessions_confirm_body"
msgid "{0} in {1} will be signed out."
msgstr "{0} ที่ {1} จะออกจากระบบ"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): body of the confirmation before signing another session out, when its location is unknown. {device} is the row's device label ("Android"), inserted as it is.
msgctxt "sessions_confirm_body_no_place"
msgid "{} will be signed out."
msgstr "{} จะออกจากระบบ"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): body of the confirmation before Sign out all other sessions. Must not say that every device is signed out: anyone who has the sign-in details can sign in again.
msgctxt "sessions_confirm_others_body"
msgid "Every other session in this list will be signed out. This session stays signed in. Anyone who knows your sign-in details can still sign in again."
msgstr "เซสชันอื่นทั้งหมดในรายการนี้จะออกจากระบบ เซสชันนี้จะยังคงลงชื่อเข้าใช้อยู่ ผู้ที่รู้ข้อมูลการลงชื่อเข้าใช้ของคุณยังลงชื่อเข้าใช้อีกครั้งได้"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): title of the confirmation before Sign out all other sessions. Cancel is the default.
msgctxt "sessions_confirm_others_title"
msgid "Sign out all other sessions?"
msgstr "ออกจากระบบเซสชันอื่นทั้งหมดหรือไม่"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): body of the confirmation before signing out the session this app is using. Confirming signs this app out.
msgctxt "sessions_confirm_self_body"
msgid "This is the session you're using. This app will be signed out."
msgstr "นี่คือเซสชันที่คุณกำลังใช้อยู่ แอปนี้จะออกจากระบบ"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): title of the confirmation before signing one session out, this app's own included. Cancel is the default.
msgctxt "sessions_confirm_title"
msgid "Sign out this session?"
msgstr "ออกจากระบบเซสชันนี้หรือไม่"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): the row's copy action (long-press or context menu item, or a copy button) that puts the full session ID on the clipboard.
msgctxt "sessions_copy_id"
msgid "Copy session ID"
msgstr "คัดลอก ID เซสชัน"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 1: the device type of a session signed in from the Android app, before its app version ("Android · 2026.10.8-1067"). The operating system's name, unchanged in every language.
msgctxt "sessions_device_android"
msgid "Android"
msgstr "Android"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 1: the device type of a session signed in from the command-line tools.
msgctxt "sessions_device_cli"
msgid "Command line"
msgstr "บรรทัดคำสั่ง"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 1: the device type of a session signed in from the iOS app, before its app version. The operating system's name, unchanged in every language.
msgctxt "sessions_device_ios"
msgid "iOS"
msgstr "iOS"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 1: the device type of a session signed in from the Linux app, before its app version. The operating system's name, unchanged in every language.
msgctxt "sessions_device_linux"
msgid "Linux"
msgstr "Linux"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 1: the device type of a session signed in from the macOS app, before its app version. The operating system's name, unchanged in every language.
msgctxt "sessions_device_macos"
msgid "macOS"
msgstr "macOS"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 1: the device type of a session that a server signed in with.
msgctxt "sessions_device_server"
msgid "Server"
msgstr "เซิร์ฟเวอร์"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 1: the device type of a session that reported no device type, or one the app does not know.
msgctxt "sessions_device_unknown"
msgid "Unknown device"
msgstr "อุปกรณ์ที่ไม่รู้จัก"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 1: the device type of a session signed in from the ur.io web app in a browser. Not tagged apple: Apple's catalog is keyed by the English source, and window_type_quality already carries "Web" there, so the apple screen reads that entry. Translated as window_type_quality is, so every platform shows the same words. The exception is Hebrew: window_type_quality's גלישה ("browsing") names the connect drawer's Web mode, so this key says ווב.
msgctxt "sessions_device_web"
msgid "Web"
msgstr "เว็บ"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 1: the device type of a session signed in from the Windows app, before its app version. The operating system's name, unchanged in every language.
msgctxt "sessions_device_windows"
msgid "Windows"
msgstr "Windows"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): shown in place of the list when it loaded with no sessions.
msgctxt "sessions_empty"
msgid "No active sessions"
msgstr "ไม่มีเซสชันที่ใช้งานอยู่"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), end of row line 3: the first 8 characters of the session ID, which the user can copy. {id} is that hex text, e.g. "01a1f3c2".
msgctxt "sessions_id"
msgid "ID {}"
msgstr "ID {}"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3, after the sign-in date: the sign-in method of a session of a client that authenticated with an API key.
msgctxt "sessions_kind_api_key_client"
msgid "API key"
msgstr "คีย์ API"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3, after the sign-in date: the sign-in method of a session created with Sign in with Apple. Not tagged apple: Apple's catalog is keyed by the English source, and apple already carries "Apple" there, so the apple screen reads that entry. Translated as apple is, so every platform shows the same words.
msgctxt "sessions_kind_apple"
msgid "Apple"
msgstr "Apple"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3, after the sign-in date: the sign-in method of a session created with an auth code made on another signed-in device or with the command-line tools. Not tagged apple: Apple's catalog is keyed by the English source, and auth_code already carries "Auth code" there, so the apple screen reads that entry. Translated as auth_code is, so every platform shows the same words.
msgctxt "sessions_kind_auth_code"
msgid "Auth code"
msgstr "รหัสยืนยัน"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3, after the sign-in date: the sign-in method of a session created when a signed-in device adopted (paired with) a discoverable device.
msgctxt "sessions_kind_device_adopt"
msgid "Device pairing"
msgstr "การจับคู่อุปกรณ์"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3, after the sign-in date: the sign-in method of a session created with Sign in with Google. Not tagged apple: Apple's catalog is keyed by the English source, and google already carries "Google" there, so the apple screen reads that entry. Translated as google is, so every platform shows the same words.
msgctxt "sessions_kind_google"
msgid "Google"
msgstr "Google"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3, after the sign-in date: the sign-in method of a session created by signing in with a password. Not tagged apple: Apple's catalog is keyed by the English source, and password_label already carries "Password" there, so the apple screen reads that entry. Translated as password_label is, so every platform shows the same words.
msgctxt "sessions_kind_password"
msgid "Password"
msgstr "รหัสผ่าน"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3, after the sign-in date: the sign-in method of a session created by signing in with the recovery phrase (an instant account's seedphrase). Each language says it as the store's seedphrase key does, the words its sign-in screen used.
msgctxt "sessions_kind_seedphrase"
msgid "Recovery phrase"
msgstr "วลีกู้คืน"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3, after the sign-in date: the sign-in method of a session created when the account itself was created.
msgctxt "sessions_kind_signup"
msgid "New account"
msgstr "บัญชีใหม่"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3, after the sign-in date: the sign-in method of a session created through single sign-on with another identity provider.
msgctxt "sessions_kind_sso"
msgid "Single sign-on"
msgstr "การลงชื่อเข้าใช้ครั้งเดียว"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3, after the sign-in date: the sign-in method of a session created by signing in with a verification code sent by email or SMS. Worded as verify_input_label, except where that reads the same as auth_code (cs, he, ja, ko, th, zh): the list can show both methods, so they must differ in every language.
msgctxt "sessions_kind_verify"
msgid "Verification code"
msgstr "รหัส OTP"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3, after the sign-in date: the sign-in method of a session created by signing in with a wallet's signature. Not tagged apple: Apple's catalog is keyed by the English source, and wallet already carries "Wallet" there, so the apple screen reads that entry. Translated as wallet is, so every platform shows the same words.
msgctxt "sessions_kind_wallet"
msgid "Wallet"
msgstr "กระเป๋า"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 2: shown instead of the Last used time when the server has no record of the session being used.
msgctxt "sessions_last_use_unavailable"
msgid "Last use unavailable"
msgstr "ไม่มีข้อมูลการใช้ล่าสุด"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 2, after the location: when the server last saw the session used. {time} is a relative time up to 7 days (the now, seconds_ago_abbrev ... days_ago_abbrev forms, e.g. "5m ago" or "now"), then a date ("Oct 3"), so the wording must read with either.
msgctxt "sessions_last_used"
msgid "Last used {}"
msgstr "ใช้ล่าสุด {}"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): footer note under the list explaining the Last used time. "Last used" is the label of sessions_last_used; say it with that key's words.
msgctxt "sessions_last_used_help"
msgid "Last used is the most recent sign-in activity the server saw. It can lag a few minutes, and the location is approximate."
msgstr "ใช้ล่าสุดคือกิจกรรมการลงชื่อเข้าใช้ครั้งล่าสุดที่เซิร์ฟเวอร์เห็น ข้อมูลอาจช้าไปไม่กี่นาที และตำแหน่งเป็นค่าโดยประมาณ"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): footer note shown when sign-ins from older app versions are not all listed yet; each appears once its sign-in renews. Must not claim that signing sessions out here ends every sign-in.
msgctxt "sessions_legacy_note"
msgid "Sign-ins from older app versions appear here once they renew. To end every sign-in, change your sign-in details."
msgstr "การลงชื่อเข้าใช้จากแอปเวอร์ชันเก่าจะแสดงที่นี่เมื่อมีการต่ออายุ หากต้องการยุติการลงชื่อเข้าใช้ทั้งหมด ให้เปลี่ยนข้อมูลการลงชื่อเข้าใช้ของคุณ"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): shown when the list failed to load the first time, above the try_again button.
msgctxt "sessions_load_failed"
msgid "Couldn't load sessions."
msgstr "โหลดเซสชันไม่ได้"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): non-blocking notice when a refresh failed. The screen keeps showing the list it had.
msgctxt "sessions_refresh_failed"
msgid "Couldn't refresh. Showing the last list."
msgstr "รีเฟรชไม่ได้ กำลังแสดงรายการล่าสุด"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): the screen's state when the account's sign-in was rejected and the user must sign in again. Generic: it names no cause. sessions_signed_out_remotely is the line for when the app knows another device signed this session out.
msgctxt "sessions_sign_in_required"
msgid "Sign in again to manage sessions."
msgstr "ลงชื่อเข้าใช้อีกครั้งเพื่อจัดการเซสชัน"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): the screen-reader action on a row that signs its session out (the row's visible control is the sign_out key). {device} is the row's device label, e.g. "Android" or "Unknown device".
msgctxt "sessions_sign_out_accessibility"
msgid "Sign out {}"
msgstr "ออกจากระบบ {}"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): the button at the bottom of the list that signs out every session except this one. Shown only when the list has this app's session and at least one other.
msgctxt "sessions_sign_out_all_others"
msgid "Sign out all other sessions"
msgstr "ออกจากระบบเซสชันอื่นทั้งหมด"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): shown under the Sign out all other sessions button when signing the other sessions out failed.
msgctxt "sessions_sign_out_others_failed"
msgid "Couldn't sign out the other sessions. Try again."
msgstr "ออกจากระบบเซสชันอื่นไม่ได้ ลองอีกครั้ง"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3: when the session was created, i.e. signed in. {date} is a localized date, e.g. "Oct 3". The sign-in method and the short ID follow: "Signed in Oct 3 · Google · ID 01a1f3c2".
msgctxt "sessions_signed_in"
msgid "Signed in {}"
msgstr "ลงชื่อเข้าใช้ {}"

#. Shown when this app was signed out because another device signed its session out on the Sessions screen (Account > Sessions). Only when the app knows that was the cause; otherwise the generic sign-in-required wording applies.
msgctxt "sessions_signed_out_remotely"
msgid "This session was signed out from another device."
msgstr "เซสชันนี้ถูกออกจากระบบจากอุปกรณ์อื่น"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): shown on a row, or on the Sign out all other sessions button, while its sign-out is pending. The control stays disabled meanwhile.
msgctxt "sessions_signing_out"
msgid "Signing out…"
msgstr "กำลังออกจากระบบ…"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): the tag on the row of the session this app is signed in with (always the first row).
msgctxt "sessions_this_session"
msgid "This session"
msgstr "เซสชันนี้"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): the screen's title, and the label of the Account row after Profile that opens it. The screen lists the account's signed-in sessions, one per signed-in app or device, and signs them out.
msgctxt "sessions_title"
msgid "Sessions"
msgstr "เซสชัน"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): shown in place of the list when the server does not support session management yet.
msgctxt "sessions_unsupported"
msgid "Sessions aren't available yet."
msgstr "ฟีเจอร์เซสชันยังไม่พร้อมใช้งาน"

#. Earnings card: the action next to set_coldkey_to_get_paid. Opens the existing coldkey setting (the connect Bittensor wallet flow).
msgctxt "set_coldkey"
msgid "Set coldkey"
msgstr "ตั้งค่า coldkey"

#. Earnings card: shown in place of sn_payout_schedule while no Bittensor coldkey is set. SN payouts go only to a coldkey; the set_coldkey action next to it opens the coldkey (connect wallet) flow.
msgctxt "set_coldkey_to_get_paid"
msgid "Set your Bittensor coldkey to get paid"
msgstr "ตั้งค่า coldkey Bittensor ของคุณเพื่อรับเงิน"

#. Account Screen
msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Settings"
msgstr "การตั้งค่า"

#. Settings row that asks the system to add the Quick Settings tile (Android 13+).
msgctxt "settings_add_quick_tile"
msgid "Add quick connect tile"
msgstr "เพิ่มไทล์เชื่อมต่อด่วน"

#. Description under the add-tile settings row.
msgctxt "settings_add_quick_tile_description"
msgid "Connect and disconnect from the Quick Settings panel and the lock screen."
msgstr "เชื่อมต่อและตัดการเชื่อมต่อจากแผงการตั้งค่าด่วนและหน้าจอล็อก"

#. Settings row that opens the widget picker to pin the app's widgets.
msgctxt "settings_add_widgets"
msgid "Add Home Screen widgets"
msgstr "เพิ่มวิดเจ็ตบนหน้าจอโฮม"

#. Description under the add-widgets settings row.
msgctxt "settings_add_widgets_description"
msgid "Quick connect, transfer balance, providers on the globe and your top contracts."
msgstr "เชื่อมต่อด่วน ยอดข้อมูลคงเหลือ ผู้ให้บริการบนลูกโลก และสัญญาหลักของคุณ"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "share"
msgid "Share"
msgstr "แชร์"

#. Button and screen title: share the known extenders as a QR code.
msgctxt "share_extenders"
msgid "Share extenders"
msgstr "แชร์ตัวขยาย"

#. How many extenders the share code carries.
msgctxt "share_extenders_count"
msgid "{} extender"
msgid_plural "{} extenders"
msgstr[0] "ตัวขยาย {} รายการ"

#. Help text on the share screen under the QR code.
msgctxt "share_extenders_hint"
msgid "Scan this code with another URnetwork app to share these extenders."
msgstr "สแกนรหัสนี้ด้วยแอป URnetwork อื่นเพื่อแชร์ตัวขยายเหล่านี้"

#. Shown on the share screen when the share payload exceeds what a QR code can hold; the text form is still offered.
msgctxt "share_extenders_too_large"
msgid "The share code is too large for a QR code. Copy the share text instead."
msgstr "รหัสแชร์มีขนาดใหญ่เกินกว่าจะเป็นรหัส QR คัดลอกข้อความแชร์แทน"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "share_logs"
msgid "Share logs"
msgstr "แชร์ไฟล์บันทึก"

